WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:04.236
-Ron Burgundy.
-What a wonderful ovation.

00:00:04.236 --> 00:00:07.507
Jimmy, do you, uh...

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:09.676
Do you mind if I just
do some stand-up comedy?

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:10.877
-[ Laughs ]
If you'd like to.

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:12.478
-Thank you.

00:00:12.478 --> 00:00:14.414
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:24.423
♪♪

00:00:24.423 --> 00:00:26.726
Thank you.
Thank you so much.

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:30.797
Oh, thank you.
That's what I'm talking about.

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:32.398
How's, uh...

00:00:32.398 --> 00:00:33.800
How's everyone doing tonight?

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.636
[ Cheers and applause ]
What? Whoa!

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:39.172
What a crowd.
What a crowd.

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:41.107
New York City in the house.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:44.143
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:44.143 --> 00:00:45.477
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.477 --> 00:00:47.346
Am I right?
Am I right?

00:00:47.346 --> 00:00:48.681
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:51.684
What does that mean, by the way,
"in the house"?

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:54.854
Are we in a house?
No, we're in a building.

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:58.324
A tall building that no one
would mistake for a house.

00:00:58.324 --> 00:00:59.459
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:02.695
New York City in the house.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:05.364
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.364 --> 00:01:08.468
How could 17 million people
fit in a house anyway?

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:09.669
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:12.238
That's a lot of toilet paper,
if you ask me.

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:17.377
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:19.845
What about an episode
of "The Real World"

00:01:19.845 --> 00:01:22.482
that took place in a house
that fit New York City?

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:23.583
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:26.752
Imagine binge-watching that.

00:01:26.752 --> 00:01:30.189
You'd be 100 before you get
halfway through episode one.

00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:32.491
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my God.

00:01:32.491 --> 00:01:35.261
-But these are the things
that keep me up at night.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:39.732
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:42.569
People like to say,
"Not in my house."

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:45.104
Well, of course not in my house.

00:01:45.104 --> 00:01:47.340
I don't know you,
so I don't want you in my house.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.008
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:50.776
Am I right or what?

00:01:50.776 --> 00:01:55.949
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:57.684
What else?
What else?

00:01:57.684 --> 00:01:59.518
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.518 --> 00:02:02.855
What else?

00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:04.557
You all having a good summer?

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:06.926
[ Cheering ]
Yeah.

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:10.663
Believe it or not, I've already
done all my Christmas shopping.

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:11.898
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:13.899
I like to get it done
before Labor Day,

00:02:13.899 --> 00:02:16.502
and I get everyone
the same thing every year --

00:02:16.502 --> 00:02:18.838
A subscription to
"Playboy" magazine.

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:20.273
[ Laughter, cheers ]

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:23.609
Oh, sure, some people complain,
and I'll tell them, "Fine.

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:26.278
I'll just leave you off the list
for next year."

00:02:26.278 --> 00:02:27.947
And they say,
"Wait! Wait, wait, wait!

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:29.915
Wait! Wait!
Wait, wait, wait!

00:02:29.915 --> 00:02:31.984
Wait, wait!
Wait, wait!

00:02:31.984 --> 00:02:33.686
Wait, wait, wait,
wait, wait, wait!

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:35.888
Just give me one more year."

00:02:35.888 --> 00:02:37.056
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:38.491
Am I right or what?

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:42.562
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:44.097
Am I right?

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:46.599
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:49.535
Show of hands -- how many
people here take the subway?

00:02:49.535 --> 00:02:51.638
Hmm? Yeah.
[ Cheers ]

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:54.540
I love the subway
whenever I come to New York.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:57.277
It's the only way
I get around town.

00:02:57.277 --> 00:02:59.912
Yeah. You know, you ever take
the subway in the summertime

00:02:59.912 --> 00:03:02.982
and you find the one car that is
empty and you think,

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:05.885
"Great. I'm gonna have
this whole car to myself,"

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:08.588
but once you get in,
you realize it is empty

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:10.657
because the air-conditioning
is broken?

00:03:10.657 --> 00:03:11.757
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.757 --> 00:03:14.594
Well, I love
to hide in that car,

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:17.263
and when people realize
they picked the hot car

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:21.701
with the broken A.C., I pop out
and say, "Hey! Surprise!"

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.035
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.035 --> 00:03:24.871
"It's hot as [bleep] in here!"

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.272
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:30.476
"Because the A.C. is broken,
and that's why it is empty."

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:34.980
[ Laughing ]
"You got tricked!

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:36.449
Let's wrestle!"

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:37.650
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:41.654
"It'll make the time go faster
for our journey."

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:43.089
Am I right or what?

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:44.256
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:44.256 --> 00:03:46.091
Am I right or what?

00:03:46.091 --> 00:03:48.728
[ Applause continues ]

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:50.296
We got any Yankee fans
here tonight?

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:53.032
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah, Yankees.

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:54.901
For those of you
who don't know baseball,

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:57.170
the New York Yankees
are a big deal.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:04:00.506
They're like the New York Jets
of baseball.

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:03.909
Just phenomenal history.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.909 --> 00:04:05.778
And, uh...
No, it's true.

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:08.314
That's nothing to laugh at.

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:10.350
I like to sit out
in the right-field bleachers

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:14.053
with all the hecklers and yell
things at opposing players.

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:16.722
Really, really
get into their heads.

00:04:16.722 --> 00:04:21.394
"Hey, number 12!
Why don't you go back to college

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:23.563
and finish your bachelor of arts
degree, huh?!"

00:04:23.563 --> 00:04:24.897
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:27.232
"There's really no excuse.

00:04:27.232 --> 00:04:29.802
You could do it online
or take night classes."

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:30.936
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.936 --> 00:04:34.173
"Or go back to school
in the off-season.

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:38.678
Hey, Mookie Betts, you're a bum!

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:40.746
In between innings,
you should read --

00:04:40.746 --> 00:04:44.783
use your time and read the
Mueller Report, unredacted!

00:04:44.783 --> 00:04:46.952
I know you won't, though.

00:04:46.952 --> 00:04:48.387
You know why?

00:04:48.387 --> 00:04:52.125
Because you're a bum!
You're a no good bum!"

00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:54.760
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:56.395
Am I right or what?

00:04:56.395 --> 00:05:01.166
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:01.166 --> 00:05:03.068
Baseball players, though.

00:05:03.068 --> 00:05:04.937
There's a weird lot.

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:09.308
What else?
Uh...

00:05:09.308 --> 00:05:11.810
Do we got any Shawn Mendes fans
here tonight?

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:14.580
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.048
Don't like him.
Never have.

00:05:16.048 --> 00:05:18.417
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.417 --> 00:05:20.786
First of all,
is he Canadian or Mexican?

00:05:20.786 --> 00:05:21.920
Make up your mind.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:23.689
You can't be both,
not in today's world.

00:05:23.689 --> 00:05:26.091
No way.

00:05:26.091 --> 00:05:29.194
Secondly,
he stole some of my songs

00:05:29.194 --> 00:05:31.998
and my singing style
when he goes to that falsetto.

00:05:31.998 --> 00:05:36.302
♪ Everything means nothing
if I can't have you ♪

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:41.107
Yeah, and I wrote that song
about Camila Cabello

00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:43.709
because she broke my heart.

00:05:43.709 --> 00:05:46.379
But now all the fans think
that he wrote it about her,

00:05:46.379 --> 00:05:48.380
but he didn't!
I did!

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:51.016
I wrote the damn song!

00:05:51.016 --> 00:05:53.552
I swear to you,
I wrote the song!

00:05:53.552 --> 00:05:57.055
And now I'm the laughingstock
of the pop-music world,

00:05:57.055 --> 00:05:59.759
and I want to tell you, Shawn,
one thing!

00:05:59.759 --> 00:06:04.029
I don't like it!
It's bush league!

00:06:04.029 --> 00:06:05.598
That's my time.

00:06:05.598 --> 00:06:07.600
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:10.703
♪♪

